+Independent re-derivation used a fresh from-scratch script `/tmp/opencode/exec_ref_depth2_20261123.py` (no reporter code, scratch files or artifacts reused; own Warshall closure, own ideal-subset DP for e, own memoised minimax for F, own child enumeration). Confirmed exactly: the n=7 cospectral pair succ P=(0x3e,0x0c,0,0,0x04,0x08,0x3e), Q=(0x3e,0x0c,0,0,0x0c,0x04,0x1e) has e(P)=e(Q)=32, F(P)=5, F(Q)=6; M1(P)=M1(Q)=(4,4,14,14,16,16,16,16,16,16,18,18,28,28); M2_struct(P)≠M2_struct(Q) with the reporter's exact first child-M1-decks P=(2,2,7,7,8,8,8,8,9,9,14,14) and Q=(2,2,6,6,7,7,9,9,10,10,14,14) (both verbatim present), plus the e=14 child decks P=(2,4,6,6,7,7,8,8,10,12), Q=(2,6,6,6,7,7,8,8,8,12) — a third independent corroboration of the companion front's tuple; refinement: first projection of the child (e, M1-deck) enumeration reproduces M1. The front's scope caveats are honest (general-poset invariant completeness; e is #P-hard, Brightwell–Winkler; soundness ≠ completeness; no transfer to S(n) without a reduction).
